Code copied or adapted from other projects is listed below with its source,
copyright and licence.

  CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md is adapted from the Contributor Covenant, version 2.1,
  https://www.contributor-covenant.org, licensed under CC BY 4.0.

  No Infisical server, SDK or CLI source code is copied into this repository,
  and nothing from Infisical's "ee/" (Infisical Enterprise licence) folders is
  used. The SDKs implement Infisical's public HTTP API from scratch. The names
  of the environment variables INFISICAL_API_URL, INFISICAL_TOKEN,
  INFISICAL_CLIENT_ID, INFISICAL_CLIENT_SECRET, INFISICAL_PROJECT_ID,
  INFISICAL_ENVIRONMENT, INFISICAL_UNIVERSAL_AUTH_CLIENT_ID and
  INFISICAL_UNIVERSAL_AUTH_CLIENT_SECRET are read for compatibility with the
  Infisical CLI (MIT).

  The AWS Signature Version 4 implementation of AwsIamAuth (all five
  languages) follows the public AWS SigV4 specification. Its unit tests use
  the example credentials and expected signatures published by Amazon Web
  Services in the AWS Signature Version 4 test suite and the AWS General
  Reference ("get-vanilla", "get-vanilla-query-order-key-case", IAM ListUsers
  2015-08-30 example), and one signature cross-checked with botocore
  (Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates, Apache License 2.0). They are
  test data only and are not part of the published packages.

  The test fixtures (the "fixtures" folders of the unit tests) are responses
  recorded from a local infisical/infisical:v0.167.10 container with every
  credential replaced by "<redacted>"; they contain no Infisical source code.
